  "development_notes": [
    "Initial CSV budget test mistakenly allowed4096bytes, which fit this small CSV. Corrected to the intended one-byte rejection. No production guard was weakened.",
    "Cross-entry-point regression exposed a Windows temporary-path overflow in a nested pixel bundle. New bundle paths use extended Windows syntax, including temporary names. Fresh and resumed reports now retain the same path representation; original exact path assertions pass.",
    "Python/CLI manifests and serialized inputs were identical, but live project revision1 reset to0 on reopen. Pixel cache identity now uses stable project identity/generation plus exact serialized input and current pixels; session revision remains an audit field. Legacy workflows retain their revision behavior.",
    "Inspection found a single-block QPS stores an effective block size smaller than the requested size. Resume now checks that canonical size and the regression runs both16 and256pixel blocks, including the default-size small-target case.",
    "Resume holds the checkpoint guard while reusing the already verified canonical scan, applies actual per-file remaining limits and actual decoded descriptor result limits, and reads descriptors without materializing a second embedded image.",
    "Initial and intermediate failure logs are preserved under build/pixel86-focused-tests.log, pixel86-final-focused-tests.log and pixel86-final3-focused-tests.log; the full regression and reported probes use the final5 release wheel."
  ]
